    {
      "id": "8ee049c1-af64-4b55-b265-f5694b91eacf",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Changing Absorption Line Profiles with OutLines to Have Same Column Densities\n\nIf `OutLines` is not installed, this can be done using `pip install SpecOutLines` in terminal or directly below. Using `pip` will automatically handle any dependencies. Detailed documentation is available at https://github.com/sflury/OutLines",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "23a4d57b-b86a-41f4-8dcf-daa5a1d926f2",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "%pip install SpecOutLines",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": "mambajs 0.19.13\n\nProcess pip requirements ...\n\nRequirement numpy already satisfied.\nRequirement scipy already satisfied.\nRequirement matplotlib already satisfied.\nSuccessfully installed SpecOutLines-1.1.0\n"
        }
      ],
      "execution_count": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "dba4c4be-fa7c-48ca-b805-6c76649f9142",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Start by importing the `OutLines` code and related basic packages.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "9b1adc7c-52c0-43fc-a547-1709a8a6ede8",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "import OutLines as OL\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 4
    },
    {
      "id": "fe2294e9-d5d0-4ee7-9e7f-0707cb53094a",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "As before, let's start by instantiating an `OutLines.Profile` object for our model.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "2891ce05-150e-44ac-b093-1bddf2be8d3d",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "wave = np.array([1548.204,1550.784])\nfosc = np.array([0.19,0.0952])\nmodel = OL.Absorption(wave,fosc,VelocityField='VelPlaw',DensityProfile='Normal')\nmodel.update_params(['TerminalVelocity','VelocityIndex'],[7000,0.5])\nmodel.update_params(['Width'],[0.1])\nmodel.update_params(['LogColumnOutflow1','LogColumnOutflow2'],[17,17])",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 44
    },
    {
      "id": "ae4edea2-9f89-4ab8-9fe5-45cec1216f48",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "Here is an example for setting the column densities of each transition equal to one another for fitting and plotting. This should be done (and only done!) for features arising from the same ion species. Below simply updates the `model` object instantiated from the `OutLines.Profile` class to update key parts of the model and fix the column densities.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "bd759ca6-76e2-4e1b-83e4-5a1ceffae317",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "from types import MethodType\nfrom numpy import array,nansum,log\n# return a profile assuming all column densities are the same\n# as the first column density\ndef Profile_sameColumns(self,wave,*pars):\n    pars = array(pars)\n    logN = pars[2]\n    pars[2:2+self.nLines] = logN\n    return self.Profile(wave,*pars)\n# convenience function\ndef get_profile(self,wave):\n    return self.Profile_sameColumns(wave,*self.get_params())\n# return a log likelihood for identical column densities\ndef log_likelihood(self,theta,x,y,yerr):\n    ybar = self.Profile_sameColumns(x,*theta)\n    ln_prb = -((y-ybar)/yerr)**2 - 2*log(yerr)\n    return nansum(ln_prb)\n# add the new profile function\nmodel.Profile_sameColumns = MethodType(Profile_sameColumns,model)\n# new get_profile\nmodel.get_profile = MethodType(get_profile,model)\n# set the new likelihood function\nmodel.log_likelihood = MethodType(log_likelihood,model)",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "fab60277-7260-4a51-b34c-a3782cc0e0b7",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "First, we need to check that everything works as intended! We can do this \nby plotting the line profile with and without the profile with and without\nthe correction we added.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "dc9884bc-32ee-4c2f-ab68-18b3d23f1fec",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "# set column densities to the same\nmodel.update_params(['LogColumnOutflow1','LogColumnOutflow2'],[16,16])\n# plot for reference\nplt.plot(w,model.get_profile(w),label='16, both same')\n# a sanity check -- make the second column density higher\nmodel.update_params(['LogColumnOutflow1','LogColumnOutflow2'],[16,17])\n# plot to compare -- should be the same!\nplt.plot(w,model.get_profile(w),ls='--',label='17, fixed same')\n# plot unfixed version -- should be different!\nplt.plot(w,model.Profile(w,*model.get_params()),ls='--',label='17, different')\nplt.xlabel(r'$\\lambda_{rest}\\rm\\:[\\AA]$')\nplt.ylabel(r'$F_\\lambda/F_{\\lambda,0}$')\nplt.legend(title=r'$\\log N_{1551}\\rm\\:[cm^{-2}]$',loc=4,frameon=False)\nplt.show()",
      "metadata": {
        "trusted": true
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "image/png": "",
            "text/plain": "<Figure size 500x450 with 1 Axes>"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "execution_count": 48
    },
    {
      "id": "502bf9a4-6984-4412-9946-12ccdedcedbc",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "As shown above, the new function `Profile_sameColumn` fixes the second line, C IV $\\lambda 1551$, to share the same column density as C IV $\\lambda 1548$ even after we've updated the parameters to disagree. But the original `Profile` does not include this correct.",
      "metadata": {}
    },
  ]
}
